  "contains_code": true,
  "description": "把中国赛区改成 KPL 的 S/A/B 分组赛制：每轮积分清零并按名次重新分组、S/A/B 各 3 个单循环（45 场）、赛季末统一 12 队双败 BO7 季后赛（16 场）+ 7-10 名排位赛、推送官方最终名次与对阵新闻、修正国际杯抽签里的挂名队和不重复席位。1.2.0 起每个赛段开始（春季赛开档、夏季赛 6/22 转会期开启）先随机抽签分成三组并推送抽签新闻；第一轮显示为「KPL 一组/二组/三组」，第二轮起才显示「KPL S组/A组/B组」，季后赛统一显示「KPL 季后赛」。命名只改显示层，不动联赛 ID、赛区和积分。1.1.0 起中国赛区（含 K 甲、青训队和所有新生成的选手）统一使用 KPL 风格中文名，能力值不变。1.2.2 起 S组/A组/B组为同一联赛级别（A 组不再被引擎视为二级联赛），不会再有 S↔A 升降级赛、降级履历和赞助层级惩罚；B↔K甲 升降级保留。1.3.0 起新增「季后赛」按钮：底部栏展开一个照原版对阵卡样式排版的完整 16 场赛程面板（轮次、日期时刻、队徽、队名、实时比分），原生联赛页/日历只有 8 个卡位、只能显示一半的问题由此绕过；同时把开赛新闻升级为完整 16 场对阵表，并在每个季后赛日结束后推送当日两场战报。1.4.0 起 16 支 KPL 队的选手名单全部换成 2026 KPL 夏季赛真实大名单（数据来源 ModelScope「2026KPL大名单选手信息」，采集自 KPL 官网）：能力值按该选手夏季赛的 KDA 排名（45%）、分均伤害排名（35%）和胜率（20%）折算，年龄按真实出生日期，潜力由年龄区间内随机生成；名单之外的替补统一降为低能力青训（能力 42-56、潜力不高于 80），保证真实首发永远是队内最强。同时修复了「同一支队每次开档选手不一样」的问题：原先按 HashMap 随机顺序分配名字，现在按队名和选手 id 固定排序，每次开档同一支队都是同一批人。建议与 KPL + Real LoL Teams 数据包一起使用。1.5.0 起能力值改为综合 2025 春 / 2025 夏 / 2025 年度总决赛 / 2026 春 / 2026 夏五个赛季的官方数据重算：分均伤害、分均承伤、伤害占比、承伤占比、经济占比、参团率、KDA、胜率、每分钟击杀、英雄池、英雄胜率共 11 项，按分路配权重（对抗路重承伤，打野重节奏，中/发育重输出，游走重参团且经济占比反向），每项在同赛季同分路内取百分位；生涯荣誉（各季官方榜单前五、总决赛冠军首发五人、总决赛 FMVP）按赛事等级和时间加权后以 18% 并入。选手名单和人名不变。1.5.0 同时禁止挂名队（TCG/ZQ/DSM 等）买人：每回合把它们的转会预算和工资预算清零，防止 AI 抢走真 KPL 队的首发。1.6.0 起统计窗口扩到 2023 春至 2026 夏共十个赛季（仍是那 11 项指标，赛季间口径差异已对齐），并把荣誉的合入方式从「按比例缩放」改成「在数据分之上加分」——旧写法会让没有冠军的选手凭空被扣 30%，数据好但无冠的选手被压掉 8-10 名。荣誉项现涵盖各季官方 9 个榜单前五、总决赛冠军首发五人、2023 夏起每届总决赛 FMVP、赛季 MVP（年度总决赛不评选赛季 MVP），以及赛季接口不覆盖的世界冠军杯（含 2023 世冠 FMVP）和挑战者杯；所有荣誉统一乘时间权重和赛事等级。结果：小胖 92（2 次 FMVP + 2 次赛季 MVP）、长生 92（2024 年度总决赛 FMVP）、轩染 91（2024 春赛季 MVP）、一诺 90（7 冠 + 2025 年度总决赛 FMVP + 2025 春赛季 MVP + 2023 世冠 FMVP + 2023 世冠冠军）。选手名单和人名依旧不变。1.6.1 修复能力值显示：引擎详情页的 OVR 实际是「11 项技能值 + 主分路」的平均（自我不计入），旧版按 ovr/80 等比缩放，五套分路模板均值只有 70-75，导致 91 分的选手详情页只显示 81，且对抗路/游走偏低最多、球员排序会变。现改为按分路模板反解缩放系数并补齐零头，详情页 OVR 与名单评分完全一致，同时保留每个位置的强弱特征。\n\nKPL (King Pro League) S/A/B format for the CN region: per-round standings reset and regrouping, three single round-robins per group (45 matches), a unified 12-team double-elimination BO7 playoff with 7-10 placement matches, official final-rank news, and international-cup seat fixes. As of 1.2.0 each split starts with a random draw into three groups (at save start for Spring, at the 6/22 transfer-window opening for Summer) with a news push; round 1 is labelled \"KPL Group 1/2/3\", rounds 2-3 use \"KPL S/A/B\", and playoffs always show \"KPL Playoffs\". Naming is display-only and never touches league ids, regions or standings. As of 1.1.0 every athlete in the CN region — including the second division, academy teams and newly generated players — gets a KPL-style Chinese name without changing any stats. As of 1.2.2 the S, A and B groups share one league tier (A is no longer a second division), so the engine no longer runs S-to-A promotion/relegation, relegation history tags or tier-based sponsor penalties; B-to-K甲 promotion is kept. As of 1.3.0 a \"Playoffs\" button opens a full 16-match bracket panel built from the game's own matchup-card layout (round, date/time, logos, names, live scores), working around the native league page and calendar only having 8 playoff slots; the bracket news now lists all 16 matches and a daily report news is pushed after each playoff day. As of 1.4.0 all 16 KPL teams use the real 2026 KPL Summer roster (source: ModelScope \"2026 KPL roster dataset\", scraped from kpl.qq.com): overall rating is derived from the player's Summer KDA rank (45%), damage-per-minute rank (35%) and win rate (20%), age from the real birth date, and potential is randomised within the player's age band. Bench players outside the roster are downgraded to low-rated academy players (42-56 overall, potential capped at 80) so the real starters always rank highest on their team. This version also fixes rosters not being stable across new saves: names used to be handed out in HashMap order, which differs every launch; assignment now follows a fixed team-name / athlete-id sort. Best used together with the KPL + Real LoL Teams data mod. As of 1.5.0 overall ratings are recomputed from five official seasons (2025 Spring, 2025 Summer, 2025 Finals, 2026 Spring, 2026 Summer) using eleven metrics — damage per minute, damage taken per minute, damage share, damage-taken share, gold share, kill participation, KDA, win rate, kills per minute, hero pool and hero win rate — percentiled within each season and lane, lane-weighted (top values tanking, jungle values tempo, mid and bot value output, support values participation with inverted gold share). Career honours (per-season official leaderboard top-fives, championship starting line-ups, Finals MVP) are event-tier and recency weighted and folded in at 18%. 1.6.1 fixes the displayed rating: the engine computes OVR as the average of the eleven skill stats plus the main-lane stat (ego is excluded), while the old code scaled the lane template by ovr/80 and the templates average only 70-75, so a 91-rated player showed as 81 in game and top/support players were penalised the most, changing the sort order. The formula now solves the scale factor per lane against the template and evens out rounding, so the in-game OVR matches the roster rating exactly while keeping each lane’s character. The player list and names are unchanged. This version also stops placeholder teams (TCG/ZQ/DSM etc.) from signing players by zeroing their transfer and salary budgets every tick, so the AI can no longer poach real KPL starters. As of 1.6.0 the window extends to ten seasons (2023 Spring through 2026 Summer, same eleven metrics, season scales aligned), and honours are now added on top of the data score instead of scaling it — the old formula shaved 30% off every player without a title, dropping strong-but-titleless players 8-10 ranks. Honours cover the official top-fives of all nine per-season leaderboards, championship starting line-ups, Finals MVP for every final since 2023 Summer, season MVP (the annual finals have no season MVP award), plus the World Champion Cup (including the 2023 KIC Finals MVP) and Challenger Cup titles the season API does not cover; everything is weighted by recency and event tier. Results: 小胖 92 (two Finals MVPs, two season MVPs), 长生 92 (2024 annual-finals MVP), 轩染 91 (2024 Spring season MVP), 一诺 90 (seven titles, 2025 annual-finals MVP, 2025 Spring season MVP, 2023 KIC Finals MVP).",
  "last_updated": "2026-10-20",
